WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.801
Video twenty. TDS: the tax that you deduct at
source.

00:00:05.001 --> 00:00:09.553
Press F11, turn on TDS, and type the TAN of
the company.

00:00:09.483 --> 00:00:13.099
Create a TDS ledger under Duties & Taxes.

00:00:13.029 --> 00:00:18.446
Give the party its PAN, its deductee type and
its nature of payment, for example rent.

00:00:18.747 --> 00:00:25.832
The ledger TDS on Rent is under Duties & Taxes. Its
type of duty is TDS, and its nature is rent.

00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:32.019
The landlord, Desai Properties, has a PAN, the
deductee type and the nature rent.

00:00:34.215 --> 00:00:42.501
Press V, then F5 for a payment. Select HDFC Bank, then Desai
Properties: ₹60,000 of rent, paid in advance.

00:00:43.328 --> 00:00:50.144
Hisaab adds the line TDS on Rent by itself:
-6,000. The bank pays ₹54,000.

00:00:50.174 --> 00:00:54.592
Type the narration, and press Ctrl+A. The
payment is saved.

00:00:57.065 --> 00:00:59.748
The rent is ₹60,000.

00:00:59.679 --> 00:01:03.564
The TDS is 10%: ₹6,000.

00:01:03.493 --> 00:01:07.844
The landlord gets ₹54,000. You pay the TDS to
the government.

00:01:08.144 --> 00:01:17.429
Alt+G, 26Q. Form 26Q, now Form 140, collects the TDS of
the quarter: ₹60,000 paid, ₹6,000 deducted.

00:01:17.459 --> 00:01:23.208
Alt+X exports the e-return. Check the file with the
government's FVU before you upload it.

00:01:23.688 --> 00:01:26.107
Next video: payroll.

